--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- WHEN ADDING A MOVE

-- Damage, Cooldown, StaminaCost must all have the same number of entries.

-- Hitbox and Animation must be folders that have 1 child per move in the combo
-- (the children must be named 1, 2, 3, etc. they correspond to the combo number)


-- !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
-- !!  IMPORTANT  !! --> IF YOU HAVE A 1 COMBO MOVE: Do not add a folder for animation or hitbox. Just name it the move name and not "1"
-- !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! --> But still have tables for every other stat (damage, cooldown, staminacost etc) so it should be a table with just one thing inside of it


-- !! TO ADD A CUSTOM HIT REACTION ANIMATION FOR WHEN A VICTIM GETS HIT !!

-- Right now, the script will look for a folder in ReplicatedStorage.Hitboxes.DefaultHitAnimations with 6 animations named 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 (will go back to 1 after 5)
-- BUT, you can make it custom. You can make a folder in ReplicatedStorage.Animations titled MoveName Hit and it will use those animations instead
-- e.g. if you have a move called "Front Kick" and you want custom hit animations, make a folder in ReplicatedStorage.Animations titled "Front KickHit"


-- TO MODIFY HITBOXLOCATIONS

-- Go to config.HitboxLocations and do the following:
